# Copy to `.env` or `.env.local` — Vite exposes only vars prefixed with `VITE_`.

# Note: the wedding seating app opens live sync with `?liveSync=1&embed=1&from=...` in a hidden iframe (no variable to set here).

# Browser-only debugging (not env): on the lottery origin run `localStorage.setItem('logLottery:liveSyncDebug', '1')` then reload — logs each applied sync (guest/table counts, latencyMs from wedding sentAt) and warns if guestCount disagrees with normalized rows (constant LIVE_SYNC_DEBUG_LS_KEY in src/utils/weddingSeatingLiveSync.ts). Remove with `removeItem`. Dev builds still log discarded stale-seq messages without this flag.

# PostMessage allowlist for wedding seating planner (import bridge + live sync). Comma-separated origins.
# Defaults include localhost ports 3000–3002, and the public seating demo https://wedding-seating-plan-pearl.vercel.app . Override in production if your wedding app origin differs.
# VITE_WEDDING_SEATING_ORIGINS=https://your-app.example.com,http://localhost:3000

# Hub links shown in the lottery UI (top-left). Override for production deploy.
# VITE_WEDDING_SEATING_URL=http://localhost:3000
# VITE_WEDDING_LOTTERY_HOME_URL=http://localhost:6719/log-lottery/home
